<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- noupdate="0" DELIBERATELY (W13) — see pb_home_hub/data/pb_sidebar.xml. -->
<odoo noupdate="0">

    <!-- SYSTEM › Settings — the cog, given a rail entry.

         Cycle 3 built the Settings hub and deliberately gave it no rail item:
         until the cutover the four SETUP items and the six ADMIN items still
         worked and a second door would have been a second answer. All ten retire
         in Cycle 5 and this is the one that replaces them, so it claims every
         one of their tags and xmlids — including the two flows that never had a
         rail entry of their own (`pb_import_connector_cockpit`, reached from
         inside Integrations, and `pb_integration_onboarding`, the stepped flow
         that replaced the connect modal), which used to leave the rail blank.

         UNGATED. The retired items carried four different gates between them and
         three of those gates were WRONG — pb_hr_payroll_base tiers over models
         whose `ir.model.access` grants read to an entirely different group
         family, so a persona holding the rail's group clicked through to an
         access dialog (W95, found live in Cycle 3). The hub asks each category's
         real question instead and renders only what this persona can open; a
         persona who can open none of them gets an explained empty state rather
         than a blank pane.

         `pb_demo` restricts this item on demo databases — see
         `pb_demo/hooks.py`, which is where the demo world's lock lives and where
         the remap from the retired ADMIN section is documented. -->
    <!-- GATED SINCE ACCESS P4 — and gated by a ROLE ALONE, which is why nothing
         is added to `groups_id` here.

         Every other entry got an older PERMISSION written into its own hub's
         data file, because the screens behind those entries already check one.
         There is no such permission for this cog: the hub is explicitly not a
         security boundary (it renders only the categories a persona can open,
         and the target actions' own ACLs are the rail), so the honest gate is
         the ACCESS TEAM ROLE — and a role can only be put on the row by
         `pb_vendor_access`, which this module must never depend on. On a build
         without the Access home this entry therefore stays as it always was.

         `restricted` is the other half of the decision. Somebody who is not on
         the access team should not simply lose the cog: they would look for it,
         not find it, and ask. Shown LOCKED they see where the setting lives and
         who to ask, in one line — which is the whole difference between a menu
         that hides things and a menu that explains itself.

         The message is written down rather than left to the default, because the
         default is the demo world's upsell ("available in the full platform"),
         and that is not true of somebody who works here and simply is not on the
         access team. -->
    <record id="item_settings" model="pb.sidebar.item">
        <field name="section_id" ref="pb_sidebar.sec_admin"/>
        <field name="restricted" eval="True"/>
        <field name="restriction_reason">Settings is looked after by the access team. This is where it lives, and they can change anything in here for you — ask them. To hand your own access to somebody covering for you, use the search box at the top and look for "Hand my access".</field>
        <field name="name">Settings</field>
        <field name="icon">settings</field>
        <field name="sequence">10</field>
        <field name="action_xmlid">pb_settings.action_pb_settings_hub</field>
        <field name="action_tag">pb_settings_hub</field>
        <field name="match_action_tags">pb_settings_hub,pb_formula_studio,pb_structures,pb_statutory,pb_integrations,pb_import_connector_cockpit,pb_integration_onboarding,pb_tenants</field>
        <field name="match_action_xmlids">base.action_res_users,base.action_res_company_form,pb_sidebar.action_pb_sidebar_item,pb_sidebar.action_pb_sidebar_section,om_hr_payroll.action_hr_payroll_configuration</field>
        <field name="match_models">hr.integration.connector,hr.formula.config,hr.payroll.structure,hr.salary.rule,vietnam.insurance.policy,vietnam.tax.table,vietnam.tax.slab</field>
    </record>

</odoo>
